  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<div align=\"center\">"
    },
    {
      "section": "🧠 dsh-local-memory",
      "text": "**Persistent cross-session local memory for DSH agents**  \n*100% Local • Plain Markdown Truth • Self-Healing SQLite Mirror • Prefix-Cache Friendly*\n\n[](https://github.com/huangjua)\n[](#)\n[](LICENSE)\n\n[Features](#-key-features) • [Quick Start](#-quick-start) • [DSH Power Suite](#-dsh-power-suite) • [Tools](#-available-tools) • [Architecture](#-architecture) • [简体中文](README_zh.md)\n\n</div>\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "💡 Why dsh-local-memory?",
      "text": "DSH agents are natively stateless. Every new conversation starts from zero, forcing you to repeatedly explain project rules, environment setups, and coding preferences."
    },
    {
      "section": "💡 Why dsh-local-memory?",
      "text": "**`dsh-local-memory` gives your agent long-term memory that you actually own:**\n- 📝 **Markdown is the Single Source of Truth**: All memories are stored in plain `.md` files under `~/.dsh/memory/`. You can view, edit, or version-control them with Git.\n- ⚡ **Zero Cache Misses**: Employs per-session frozen snapshots (`WeakMap<Session, ...>`) to maintain byte-for-byte prefix cache stability, saving tokens and speeding up responses.\n- 🔒 **100% Local & Fail-Closed**: No cloud leaks. Workspace boundaries strictly validated against official workspace registries.\n- 🛡️ **Staged Write Approvals**: Global profile edits require explicit user confirmation (`memory_pending approve`) to prevent hallucinated changes."
    },
    {
      "section": "💡 Why dsh-local-memory?",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Installation",
      "text": "```bash"
    },
    {
      "section": "In your DSH plugin environment",
      "text": "dev_inject_plugin @dsh-external/dsh-local-memory\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Typical Usage Flow",
      "text": "1. **Ask agent to remember**: *\"Remember that our project uses pnpm and strict TypeScript.\"*\n2. **Review staged memory**: Run `/local-memory` or approve staged entries via `memory_pending`.\n3. **Seamless recall**: In any new session, the agent automatically receives the frozen memory context without any extra prompts.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "🧩 DSH Power Suite",
      "text": "This plugin is part of the **DSH Agent Power Suite** — 4 modular, zero-hard-dependency plugins forming a complete closed-loop developer workflow:\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    M[\"🧠 dsh-local-memory<br>(1. Remember rules & prefs)\"] --> E[\"⚡ dsh-context-economy<br>(2. Save 80%+ tokens reading code)\"]\n    E --> A[\"🛡️ dsh-evidence<br>(3. Tamper-proof audit receipts)\"]\n    A --> S[\"🔍 dsh-session-index<br>(4. CJK search & bookmarks)\"]"
    },
    {
      "section": "🧩 DSH Power Suite",
      "text": "| Plugin | Role in Suite | Synergy with Local Memory |\n|---|---|---|\n| 🧠 **[dsh-local-memory](https://github.com/huangjua/dsh-local-memory)** | **Memory Layer** (Current) | Curates persistent long-term knowledge, developer profiles, and workspace conventions. |\n| ⚡ **[dsh-context-economy](https://github.com/huangjua/dsh-context-economy)** | **Context Economy** | Slashes code reading tokens by 80–93%, leaving ample prompt budget for memory snapshots. |\n| 🛡️ **[dsh-evidence](https://github.com/huangjua/dsh-evidence)** | **Audit & Receipts** | Creates SHA256 receipts for execution runs, grounding memory entries in verifiable evidence. |\n| 🔍 **[dsh-session-index](https://github.com/huangjua/dsh-session-index)** | **Session Search** | Indexes raw `.jsonl.zstd` logs with CJK support. Memory curation belongs here; log searching belongs there. |"
    },
    {
      "section": "🧩 DSH Power Suite",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "section": "📖 Deep Dive & Reference",
      "text": "<details>\n<summary><b>🛠️ Available Tools & Commands (8 Tools + 1 Command)</b></summary>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Tools",
      "text": "| Tool | Description | Scope / Action |\n|---|---|---|\n| `memory_write` | Add a new memory entry | User/Profile ➡️ Staged; Workspace ➡️ Direct |\n| `memory_update` | Revise an entry via `memoryId` or `oldText` | Previous active marked `superseded` |\n| `memory_forget` | Remove an entry from active memory | Replaced with minimal tombstone |\n| `memory_pending` | Manage staged approvals | `list`, `approve`, `reject` |\n| `memory_append_daily`| Append timestamped block to daily notes | Append-only workspace scratchpad |\n| `memory_search` | Search memories with FTS5 trigram | Auto pre-syncs modified Markdown |\n| `memory_status` | Detailed file counts, active entries, DB size | Read-only diagnostics |\n| `memory_distill` | Collect candidate daily notes for distillation | Read-only + state metadata |"
    },
    {
      "section": "User Commands",
      "text": "- `/local-memory feedback <receipt-id> bundle <helpful|harmful>`: Submit feedback on memory delivery receipts.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>📁 Architecture & Storage Layout</b></summary>\n\n```text\n~/.dsh/memory/\n├── user/                       # User-level profile & global memories (MEMORY.md / USER.md)\n├── workspaces/<WorkspaceId>/   # Workspace-scoped memories (MEMORY.md)\n├── daily/<WorkspaceId>/        # Daily scratch notes (YYYY-MM-DD.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "User Commands",
      "text": "**Key Architectural Invariants:**\n- **Markdown is the Single Source of Truth**: All text and metadata reside in `.md` files.\n- **SQLite is a Disposable Replica**: If corrupted, SQLite automatically recovers from Markdown via `buildMemoryIndex`.\n- **Pre-Search Incremental Sync**: `memory_search` syncs changed files on the fly by `content_hash`.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>⚖️ Design Trade-offs & Boundaries</b></summary>"
    },
    {
      "section": "User Commands",
      "text": "| Advantage | Trade-off / Boundary |\n|---|---|\n| SSOT/Replica separation ensures zero data loss | Schema v12 migration chain requires strict maintenance |\n| Dual channel: frozen snapshots + real-time tool search | Local-machine bound (no cloud sync) |\n| Strict workspace fail-closed isolation | Index contains plain text (do not use on untrusted shared machines) |\n| 566 test cases with comprehensive coverage | `forget` removes active surfaces, does not do physical disk shredding |\n\n</details>"
    },
    {
      "section": "User Commands",
      "text": "<details>\n<summary><b>🧪 Building & Testing</b></summary>\n\n```bash"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install dependencies",
      "text": "pnpm install --frozen-lockfile"
    },
    {
      "section": "Build TypeScript to lib/",
      "text": "bash scripts/build.sh"
    },
    {
      "section": "Typecheck & Run test suite",
      "text": "npm run typecheck\nnpm test\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>🙏 Credits & References</b></summary>"
    },
